id: H09
target: src/sello/private/sha512.nim
desc: finish: FIPS 180-4 Sec 5.1.2's 128-bit big-endian message-bit-length field assembly ("site 3") -- the high and low halves swapped, 'ctx.buffer[112 + i] = byte((bitsHi shr ...))' / 'ctx.buffer[120 + i] = byte((bitsLo shr ...))' -> bitsLo written to the leading (112) half and bitsHi to the trailing (120) half, so every padded message's encoded bit-length is wrong except the unreachable case bitsHi == bitsLo. The RFC-006 slice 4 list's named padding length-encoding-error mutant.
====OLD====
  for i in 0 ..< 8:
    ctx.buffer[112 + i] = byte((bitsHi shr (56 - i * 8)) and 0xFF'u64)
  for i in 0 ..< 8:
    ctx.buffer[120 + i] = byte((bitsLo shr (56 - i * 8)) and 0xFF'u64)
====NEW====
  for i in 0 ..< 8:
    ctx.buffer[112 + i] = byte((bitsLo shr (56 - i * 8)) and 0xFF'u64)
  for i in 0 ..< 8:
    ctx.buffer[120 + i] = byte((bitsHi shr (56 - i * 8)) and 0xFF'u64)
====END====
